CommitDate: Sun Jun 21 13:42:49 2026 -0400

    perf: 2x batch sizes + batch-aware VRAM footprint for higher decode throughput
    
    Measured the generation path: decode is memory-bandwidth-bound and ran at only
    ~70 tok/s (15% GPU util) at the old batch sizes -- well below the card's ceiling.
    Doubled the per-model batches for small/mid models (128/96/64/40) and modestly
    for 32B (12->16, VRAM-limited); the OOM-microbatch-split backstops any overshoot.
    Made estimate_footprint_gb batch-aware (weights + 0.018*params*batch + 2.5) so
    the scheduler packs correctly with the larger KV cache (32B solo ~76 GB; the
    small/mid tail still packs ~4-wide under the 0.88 budget).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

